Direct machine-code encoding into an in-memory buffer:

libhymir/       # MIR types, IR->MIR lowering — pure C, no target knowledge
libhyregalloc/  # linear scan over MIR, target owns register set
libhyx64/       # x86-64 encoder: MIRValue+op -> bytes+relocs
libhyobj/       # ELF (and later PE/Mach-O) writer, takes bytes+relocs+symbols
